<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="033" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Policy &amp; Procedures module (submit/read on the framework)</title>
    <phase>P3 Legal Front Door intake MVP</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:031</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Thin request type on the 031 framework (config + form, submit/read only) — no new endpoint group, no workflow; STANDARD per CLAUDE.md §8. Note: it does modify .tsx, but the change is additive config on an established, tested framework with no authz-state logic.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Simplest module — a single-step submit/read request type; no open decisions.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>P&amp;P-specific config/form; disjoint from 032's NDA files; both build on the stabilized 031 framework.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031</deps>
    <tags>frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Implement the Policy &amp; Procedures (P&amp;P) request type on the 031 typed-intake framework: a submit form (FormModal single-step, or WizardModal if multi-field review is warranted) and a read/status view. This is the simplest Front Door module — submit + read on the framework, no approval workflow (FR-16).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Fluent v9 + React 18 on @spaarke/ui-components.</role>
  <goal>An employee can submit a Policy &amp; Procedures request through the framework and view its status. P&amp;P is registered as a request type (config + form) per FR-14 — no new endpoint group, no new SPA, no bespoke Dialog.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-16: A submit/read Policy &amp; Procedures module on the framework; an employee submits a P&amp;P request and views status. UX brief §3 typed intake: single-step types use FormModal; multi-step use WizardModal. This is the lightest request type — no review/approval workflow (unlike NDA). It reuses the 031 submit + get-status endpoints and the sprk_servicerequest schema from 030 (requesttype=PolicyProcedures).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md (§3 typed intake row; §4 nine states)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/** — the 031 request-type registry + typed-intake driver (register PolicyProcedures here)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/index.ts:273 (FormModal, WizardModal presets)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md (FR-16)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>031 (typed-intake framework) must be complete. 030 supplies the PolicyProcedures option-set value + status. Parallel with 032 (NDA) — disjoint files.</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">P&amp;P MUST be added as a request type on the 031 framework (registry entry + form/schema) using FormModal (single-step) or WizardModal — no new endpoint group, no new SPA, no hand-rolled Dialog (§11 + ADR-050).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">P&amp;P is submit/read only — do NOT add a review/approval workflow or status transitions beyond submit → (in-progress) → viewable status (FR-16; contrast NDA FR-15).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; renders in light, dark, and Teams theme at narrow width; zero hardcoded hex.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/modal-shell.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Request-type registration" location="src/client/external-spa (031 registry)">Register PolicyProcedures = { id:'PolicyProcedures', mode:'form', form/schema }.</pattern>
      <pattern name="SprkModal presets" location="docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md">FormModal for a single-step P&amp;P submit; Cancel always left.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load FR-16, ux-brief §3/§4, and the 031 framework registry. Confirm the PolicyProcedures option-set value from 030.</step>
    <step order="2">Client: register PolicyProcedures as a request type with a FormModal single-step form (fall back to WizardModal only if the fields warrant a review step).</step>
    <step order="3">Client: wire submit (reuse 031 submit) + a read/status view for the submitter.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the nine ux-brief §4 states for the P&amp;P surfaces. Client test: P&amp;P form renders in FormModal; submit succeeds; status view renders.</step>
    <step order="5">Build: npm run build:prod (client). No BFF change expected — if any, /conflict-check + publish delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the external-spa client (build:prod)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Only if a BFF change is unavoidable</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/** — PolicyProcedures request-type registration (FormModal) + read/status view</output>
    <output type="test">client tests — P&amp;P form render + submit + status view</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an employee, when they submit a P&amp;P request via FormModal, then a sprk_servicerequest with requesttype=PolicyProcedures is created and the submitter can view its status.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given P&amp;P is added, when reviewing the diff, then it is a registry entry + form/schema on the 031 framework — no new endpoint group, no new SPA (FR-14).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: P&amp;P has NO review/approval workflow — it is submit/read only (FR-16); no approval UI in the diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the P&amp;P surfaces, when rendered in light/dark/Teams theme at narrow width, then semantic tokens adapt with zero hardcoded hex and no console errors.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Renders P&amp;P intake + status">
      <steps><step>Open intake, pick Policy &amp; Procedures</step><step>Complete the FormModal form and submit</step><step>View the submitted request status</step></steps>
      <expected>Form + status render; submit succeeds; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode + Teams theme (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode; load in Teams theme</step><step>Verify tokens adapt</step></steps>
      <expected>Zero hardcoded hex; adapts; readable at narrow Teams width</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <notes>Spec FR-16. UX brief §3 (typed intake). Lightest module — submit/read only, no workflow. Parallel with 032 (NDA) in group D; keep P&amp;P files disjoint from NDA. Reuse the 031 submit/status endpoints; do not add BFF surface unless unavoidable.</notes>
